proposed change to speed limits is  coming to a northwest valley area mary  jane belliesa takes us to the desert  shores community on buffalo and cheyenne  with how homeowners are responding to  the change  the temporary speed limit sign in the  desert shores community is posted as 30  miles per hour residents say it's a much  needed change from the 35 mile per hour  speed limit as many drivers are seen  speeding through the neighborhoods  to mitigate excessive speeding the city  of las vegas conducted a speed study in  the community it was temporarily reduced  to 30 miles per hour the city recommends  keeping it to 30 miles per hour to  promote safer roadways resident  catherine morales agrees 30 is fine for  around here  and people are very careful they stop if  somebody's crossing the road i don't see  any real issues there but some other  residents like david colemeyer wanted to  be 25. i think a lot of communities are  between 15 to 25.  i think there's a lot of people that are  driving very reckless around in general  you also have a lot of animals that are  running around whether it's the ducks  and so on and a lot of times you will  see  deceased animals along the roadway  jonathan alvarez oversees security for  the community's business center we have  so many walkers joggers individuals  walking their dogs wildlife that crosses  the street with the amount of lakes  there are around here so the streets are  busy i highly encourage them to keep the  speed limit as it is you can submit a  speed limit change online through the  city's website and the city will conduct  a traffic study this review includes  looking at existing conditions and  future developments reporting from  cheyenne and buffalo mary jane vallieza  8 news now  the traffic parking commission will  discuss the change in other agenda items  tomorrow afternoon at 1 p.m at city hall
 

